# A1: the AUDITED attach on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic-roundhost-audit (the control's profile plus the three levers, the lean log and QWEN_FAST_TP4_ROUND_HOST_AUDIT=1: the reference runs beside the selection, the merge and the keyed write on
# the live data and the two must agree byte for byte; a difference uses the reference's bytes and fails the arm). Host work only: no device audit is added, no trace or allocation changes. Tests: warmup, one coding stream,
# concurrent4_steady (one block, one quad: the four-live round), concurrent8_steady (both blocks and both quads: the quad-blocks smoke rule needs it) and eight 32k code users.
# READ, in order, stopping at the first failure: (1) the attach: ONE '[PINDIAG] round host engaged log=1 select=1 read=1 keyed=1 lean=1 audit=1' line, no 'refused' and no 'declined' line;
# (2) c2_smoke_check clean (its round_host rules: the ledger line a step with every field, SELECT and READ on 95% of the drafting steps, the keyed write on half of the verifies of a block, the feature guard skipped on
# some steps once 64 reads have passed, none of the lines LEAN drops, an '[ROUND-HOST-AUDIT] kind=select|merge|keyed equal=1' line for each lever and ZERO equal=0); (3) the ledger itself:
# python3 scripts/ci/round_host_report.py summary <server log> --live 8 (and --live 4): every phase has a number. The answers' hashes are NOT compared here (the audit hands the reference's bytes on a
# difference, so equality proves nothing about the arm): E2 against E1 is the exactness read. Duration (estimate): 90 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/round-host window (docs/tp4-round-host.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/round-host and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the NEEDS graph and every read rule.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-rh-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/round-host commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-rh-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-traffic-roundhost-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_steady,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k
